    "body": "## Summary\n- Keep the original Rayhan battle card visible, including its attack and selected counterargument, while the scripted vote remains owned by Events.\n- Persist a randomized 2:2 first-four vote order and reserve vote five for the player; preserve the existing 3–4 second delays and reload progress.\n- Put the current player first in the Rayhan Event title, remove the irrelevant resolved warning, and announce the player as winner only for this scripted tutorial result.\n- Disable manual voting in the guided tutorial at both UI and action layers, unlocking normal votes from the canonical first-independent-battle completion flag.\n- Keep exact Web/docs mirrors and refresh cache-busting references for changed scripts.\n\n## Validation\n- PASS: controller regression, including all six first-four permutations, five separate votes, 2:2 after vote four, 3:2 final tally, persisted sequence/progress, reload after two votes, and no generic battle crowd timer.\n- PASS: Rayhan reveal, post-win sequence, post-result, missing-group, generic Events, Nastya crowd/timing, boot routing, and boot mirror regressions.\n- PASS: JS syntax, cache-independent Node test syntax, diff check, and six byte-identical Web/docs mirror pairs.\n- BLOCKED locally: tools/test_stage7_15_rayhan_result_card_dom.mjs cannot launch its Playwright Chromium process in this environment; the automatic review rejected that launch because the active browser policy requires the built-in Codex Browser. The DOM assertions are updated and syntax-checked; no Safari/runtime acceptance is claimed.\n\nDraft pending DOM regression/CI review.",
